       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION. 
       PROGRAM-ID.      RSO29GCH.   
       AUTHOR.          Michael O. Evert.   
       DATE-WRITTEN.    September 2000. 
       DATE-COMPILED.   TODAY.  
      ******************************************************************
      *                         RSO29GCH

      * 
      *  The purpose of this subroutine is to write out history 
      *  records reflecting the changes made to an input IBR (cabin 
      *  berthing) and all its guests.  
      * 
      *  This subroutine will compare two versions of IBR level data
      *  and guest level data for a given cabin/IBR. This subroutine
      *  will only be called when an existing IBR has been changed. 
      *  It will not be called to write history for new or cancelled
      *  berthings. 
      * 
      *  So this subroutine can determine the changes, a before and 
      *  after picture of the IBR and guests in two copies of the   
      *  RSP06GCI proc layout.  It also needs a before and after
      *  picture of TPR records referenced by the IBR.  
      * 
      *  Protocol for calling subroutine:   
      * 
      *      CALL 'RSO29GCH'      USING DPP01-COMMON-DATA-FIELDS
      *                                 DPP01-COMMON-INFO   
      *                                 RSP06-OLD   
      *                                 RSP06-NEW   
      *                                 RSP29-AUXILIARY-INPUT.  
      * 
      ******************************************************************
      *    Modifications
      ******************************************************************
      *    20190801 RAE  Re-written.
      ******************************************************************
